RViz on QNX: OpenGL ES 2/3 on Screen through OGRE's GLES2 render system.

QNX has no desktop OpenGL and no GLX/X11, only OpenGL ES through EGL on
Screen.
- rviz_ogre_vendor: build OGRE's GLES2 render system (with the QNX EGL
  support of patches/0100-qnx-screen-egl-gles2.patch) instead of the GL one,
  and the RTShader System; leave out the OGRE components RViz does not use.
  Its CMake extras: no OpenGL/X11 link on QNX, and an imported
  rviz_ogre_vendor::OgreRTShaderSystem target.
- rviz_rendering: load RenderSystem_GLES2 and accept "OpenGL ES" as the
  renderer; no GLX dummy context and no X11 headers. GL ES has no
  fixed-function pipeline, and OGRE draws every viewport in the RTShader
  System's scheme there, so initialise the shader generator (its shader
  library is in rviz_ogre_vendor's share/OGRE/Media), resolve that scheme's
  techniques from a material's default one (what OgreBites'
  SGTechniqueResolverListener does), and register RViz's scene managers
  with it. An ES 2.0 version maps to "GLSL 1.10": do not refuse to start.
- RenderWindow is an OpenGL-surface QWindow on QNX: Qt's qnx platform gives
  a raster window buffers of its own and draws into them; OGRE creates the
  window's buffers and EGL surface itself (on the screen_window_t that
  QWindow::winId() is).

Upstream-Status: Pending
